# w4_heat_plate.shape -- the vector check of W4's red-black selection store (docs/DESIGN.md 2.12.10
# "What runs fused" and "The vector check", Decision 108, lead decision L-fl). Written by hand from
# the spec, never from the compiler's output. Format: see tests/shape.sh's header.
program ports/w4_heat_plate.sea

# 2.12.10: rb_half_sweep (lines 254-263 of the port: its fn line to its closing brace) is inlined
# into the main program at both call sites (class (c) of LANGUAGE.md 8.6), and inlined code keeps
# its callee's lines (L-fl). Its fused selection store T[1..ny-1, :] = where(colorIn, Tn, Tc)
# (F1 (3), (5)) runs in a 2-lane loop on arm64 and in both the 4-lane and the 2-lane loop on x86_64.
vector arm64 .main 261 261 sel
vector x86_64 .main 261 261 sel
